# patches/xlibre-xserver/series: applied in order with patch -p1.
#
# FreeBSD's port (x11-servers/xlibre-server/files, ports commit 956f979f48)
# carries 8 patches for the server (E23 D11); the port builds 25.1.9, the
# version pinned here. 4 are needed and carried, each with its Origin; all 4
# apply to 25.1.9 exactly as the port has them (0002 and 0004 had been rebased
# for 25.2.2 and are the port's hunks again). 0004 is still needed: 25.1.9's
# meson.build adds the same host epoll-shim include path.
0001-config-udev-kbdmux-and-no-evdev-drivers.patch
0002-bsd_init-raw-console-keyboard-while-X-owns-the-VT.patch
0003-os-support-build-SlowBcopy-on-BSD.patch
0004-meson-epoll-shim-include-path-from-its-dependency.patch
#
# The other 4 are not carried:
#   patch-hw_xfree86_os-support_shared_seatd-libseat.c
#       25.1.9 lacks it (the XSERVER_PLATFORM_BUS guards; 25.2.x has them),
#       but it only changes shared/seatd-libseat.c, which is compiled only
#       with -Dseatd_libseat=true; seatd is off here.
#   patch-hw_xfree86_xorg-wrapper.c, patch-hw_xfree86_meson.build
#       both touch the suid wrapper (Xorg.wrap), which is not built
#       (-Dsuid_wrapper=false; X is started as root by launchd/loginwindow).
#   patch-os-utils.c
#       CLOCK_MONOTONIC_COARSE -> CLOCK_MONOTONIC_FAST. NextBSD's
#       <sys/_clock_id.h> defines CLOCK_MONOTONIC_COARSE as
#       CLOCK_MONOTONIC_FAST, so upstream's code already uses the same clock.
# The port's post-patch sed on config/meson.build (lines 31-54) drops the
# install of upstream's NVIDIA xorg.conf.d snippets. It is not a patch here:
# build-xlibre.sh removes those files after meson install instead (the same
# rm it did on 25.2.2, where they came from hw/xfree86/compat); 10-quirks.conf,
# installed by the same block, stays.
#
# NextBSD's own, after the port's:
#   0005  -launchd <name>: take the listening sockets from launchd, so the
#         org.nextbsd.xlibre LaunchAgent can start the server when the first
#         X client connects (nextbsd/nextbsd-xlibre#13, the XQuartz model).
#         A socket's private directory must be the real uid's (getuid),
#         since Xorg is set-uid root (nextbsd/nextbsd-xlibre#20).
0005-os-listen-on-launchd-sockets.patch
#   0006  -Ddri_driver_path: GLX's DRI driver directory set explicitly, not
#         dri.pc's dridriverdir, which pkgconf prefixes with the build
#         sysroot (nextbsd/nextbsd-xlibre#20).
0006-meson-dri_driver_path-option.patch
